<br>
In the SEMI Lab, we design and develop <strong>smart materials and intelligent structures</strong> with integrated sensing, energy, and functional capabilities. Leveraging advanced and additive manufacturing, we embed sensors, energy harvesting and storage components, and functional materials within metallic, polymeric, composite, and textile-based structures to enable <strong>self-powered sensing, real-time structural health monitoring, and adaptive functionality</strong>. Our research spans triboelectric nanogenerators, embedded and printed sensors, electronic textiles, and multifunctional structures, advancing <strong>resilient, sustainable, and intelligent systems</strong> for aerospace, defense, space, and other emerging applications. <br>
<br>

<b>Our Current Research Directions:</b>
<ul>
  <li><b>3D-printed smart structures with integrated and embedded sensing capabilities</b></li>
  <li><b>Smart and self-powered materials, surfaces, and structures</b></li>
  <li><b>Triboelectric nanogenerators for energy harvesting and self-powered sensing</b></li>
  <li><b>Printed and embedded sensors for real-time structural health monitoring</b></li>
